<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>Analyzing Various Quadratic Expressions</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02250</md:content-id>
    <md:title>Analyzing Various Quadratic Expressions</md:title>
    <md:uuid>2fc9a1d5-b31e-4425-a493-d94aef8ab615</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section class="numbered-exercises" id="sect-00001">
      <title>Warm Up</title>
      <!--Text
      Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00001">
        <problem id="prob-00001">
          <para id="para-00001">Examine the four expressions below. Which one doesn't belong?</para>
          <table class="unnumbered" id="table-00001">
            <tgroup cols="4">
              <tbody>
                <row>
                  <entry>
<para id="para-00002">A. <m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
<para id="para-00003">B. <m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
                <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                <m:mn>8</m:mn>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                <m:mn>5</m:mn>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
<para id="para-00004">C. <m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
                <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                <m:mn>25</m:mn>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
<para id="para-00005">D. <m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
                <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                <m:mn>3</m:mn>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
                  </entry>
                </row>
              </tbody>
            </tgroup>
          </table>

          <para id="para-00006">There are many possible answers for which equation does not belong
            in a group with the others. Determine which equation you think should be eliminated and
            explain your reasoning.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">

          <para id="para-00008">Compare your answer: </para>
          <para id="para-00009">Equation A: The only expression that is not in standard form. Or,
            when written in standard form, it is the only one that has an even number for the
            constant term.</para>
          <para id="para-00010">Equation B: The only expression in standard form that has a leading
            coefficient other than 1.</para>
          <para id="para-00011">Equation C: The only expression in standard form that doesn't have
            three terms. It is the only one without a linear term.</para>
          <para id="para-00012">Equation D: The only expression in standard form that can't be
            written in factored form. It is prime.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
    </section>
  </content>
</document>